WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.110
- Ladies and gentlemen, we're
sending over 30% of our kids

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:05.360
to the Ivy Leagues, baby.

00:00:06.329 --> 00:00:07.950
- [Student] He does everything
to get us to college.

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:10.890
- It's not a normal school.

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:14.343
- All that I care about is winning.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:19.830
- [Interviewer] Do you have any texts

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.990
from a loved one that passed away?

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:22.823
- I do.

00:00:22.823 --> 00:00:23.910
- I do.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:24.743
- Yeah.

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:32.640
- Yes, my best friend. His name is Angel.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.580
He passed away in 2019.

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:37.800
- What was your favorite memory with him?

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:38.820
- Oh, there's a lot.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:41.490
So the first time we went to a concert,

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:44.550
and it was like our first
time, like, you know,

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:45.900
trying to buy alcohol.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.390
That's where, like I
realized like, okay you know,

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:50.220
yeah, this guy's gonna be my partner

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:51.990
where we're gonna get
into a lot of trouble.

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:55.710
He text me saying a doctor
told him that he had leukemia.

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:59.820
That's where he sent
me like his last text.

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:02.100
I know this is random but
if anything happens to me,

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.350
like if I die, I just want you to know

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:06.180
that you've always been my best friend.

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:08.700
And if anything happens
to me, do me a favor

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.930
and watch out for Allison
and Treasa for me.

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:14.310
We never had all this bromance,

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:16.452
like, oh, I love you bro, this and that.

00:01:16.452 --> 00:01:18.960
I did realize like, oh shoot,
like, this is happening.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:21.090
And then I said, don't say that yet.

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:22.920
Say that in the next 50 years.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:25.983
And that was it. That was
my last message to him.

00:01:26.852 --> 00:01:28.110
But I do have one video.

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:32.613
He was passed out. I was
drawing something on his neck.

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:35.943
- You gotta use your words,
you can't do this to me.

00:01:35.943 --> 00:01:38.016
- A little touch up there.

00:01:38.016 --> 00:01:41.433
Do you wanna sit up? Do you wanna sit up?

00:01:44.007 --> 00:01:46.230
- Yeah. To be honest, I am tearless,

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:49.473
I've cried so many times. I
don't think I can cry anymore.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:54.870
- Her name is Blue Roxy
Scott, she's my best friend,

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:58.830
and she passed away in
2020 from cystic fibrosis.

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:00.510
For her whole life,

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:03.960
I've known that she wasn't
going to live very long,

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:07.320
so the text messages are
just me talking to her

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:09.180
like I would talk to her any other day.

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:14.180
So, on September 18th I said,
hey, do you have any idea

00:02:14.503 --> 00:02:15.930
how I make skinny jeans cool?

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:18.840
And she goes, hmm, maybe a cute belt

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:20.400
with a big shirt tucked in the front.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.170
And I go, wow, that was some good advice.

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:23.310
I didn't expect that.

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:25.382
And she just said, LOL.

00:02:25.382 --> 00:02:27.780
And then I text her, hi, I
love you, you're a rockstar.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.340
You got this.

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:31.503
And she never responded.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:35.160
I feel connected to her all the time,

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:37.680
but especially like watching sunset

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:39.864
always makes me feel connected to her,

00:02:39.864 --> 00:02:43.096
anytime I'm at the beach
or just re-watching videos.

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:44.202
- Just kidding Meghan, I love you.

00:02:44.202 --> 00:02:45.035
You brought me pie last night.

00:02:45.035 --> 00:02:46.413
- Wait, what?

00:02:46.413 --> 00:02:48.531
- Yeah. She brought us pie.

00:02:48.531 --> 00:02:50.250
- That was just at the
beginning, her saying like

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:51.210
that she loves me.

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:54.120
She wasn't very like, open
about those sort of things.

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:57.180
So to like have her voice on
video saying that she loves me

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:58.533
is like super special.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:02.970
So today I'm talking
about my friend, Angie.

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:06.480
We met at the top of 2019
and right away we vibed.

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:07.950
My favorite memory with Angie

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:11.428
was actually at my 20th birthday party.

00:03:11.428 --> 00:03:12.660
At the end of the party she went up to me

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:15.487
and she was just like,
thank you so, so, so much

00:03:15.487 --> 00:03:17.160
for inviting me. Like, I'm so glad I came.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:19.555
She really needed that and everything,

00:03:19.555 --> 00:03:20.748
and I was really glad to like

00:03:20.748 --> 00:03:22.410
bring some like light and life into her.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:24.240
So yeah, the last couple ones,

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:26.416
the first she wished me happy birthday,

00:03:26.416 --> 00:03:27.510
she was like, enjoy yourself fully.

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:30.868
And I was like, thanks Ang!
Miss you, come through tonight.

00:03:30.868 --> 00:03:32.730
And she was like, I can
get outta work at eight,

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:33.900
you think I can still slide?

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:35.100
And I was like, hell yeah.

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:37.350
Like you'll probably just
miss the food, but that's all.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:38.970
And then she was like, sounds good.

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:41.820
And that was the last
message I had from her.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:44.820
So it wasn't until my second
day of my last semester

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:48.597
at Santa Ana that our mutual
friend Candace goes up to me

00:03:48.597 --> 00:03:50.637
and she goes "Did you hear about Angie?"

00:03:52.193 --> 00:03:53.893
She was like, "Angie passed away".

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:57.480
And it was really hard

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:01.500
because she told me February 12th, 2020,

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:05.400
and Angie had passed
away January 12th, 2020.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:08.490
So like, I didn't get
to go to her funeral.

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:10.143
I didn't get any type of closure,

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:14.460
but I had a lot of film
rolls from my birthday party.

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:17.280
And so I was like, I need
to develop all of them.

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:19.050
I need to develop for them now.

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:22.110
This is Angie. This is my
favorite picture of her.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:24.660
I took the picture and I just like

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:26.580
think of the last thing she said to me,

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:29.370
and I think of like,
just how happy she was.

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:31.680
And it's just really nice
to be a light like that

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:33.150
in other people's lives.

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:37.920
- My dad was a very intense
kind of like big personality,

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:40.020
vivacious type of person.

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:42.259
He dealt with a lot of anger issues.

00:04:42.259 --> 00:04:45.900
A lot of that stemmed
from, had the childhood

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:48.090
that he had to endure growing up.

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:50.490
He would try to reach out to me a lot

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.410
and I didn't really wanna talk to him,

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:55.650
but the last time he
reached out, I was like,

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:57.180
I'm gonna assert myself

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:59.790
and I'm not gonna text
back until I want to.

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:01.530
And that was a few days before he passed.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:04.860
He said, I know you're probably busy

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:07.320
but just wanted to say hi and I love you.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:10.320
And then he said, why
you no say love you dad?

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:12.150
With like a crying emoji.

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:14.410
And I said, I love you too,

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:15.810
sometimes when I get
messages before meetings

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:18.420
or read them right when I
wake up, I forget to respond.

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:21.360
And then in the morning he said

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:23.940
love you and have a less
stressful day punkins,

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:26.771
which was a nickname he
called me with some emojis,

00:05:26.771 --> 00:05:29.040
and said love you too, I'm
hoping it's less stress.

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:31.740
And then he said, my buddy
had me covered for three days,

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:35.070
beer emoji, thumbs up, laughing emoji,

00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:39.321
and I'd send a pot leaf,
but I don't have that emoji.

00:05:39.321 --> 00:05:40.803
And I said, LOL sadly.

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:45.633
And then that was it. Just like benign.

00:05:47.733 --> 00:05:49.380
But it's weird that the last
thing I ever said to him

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:50.823
was the word sadly.

00:05:51.842 --> 00:05:53.120
- [Interviewer] Yeah?

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:54.690
- Yeah, just weird.

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:59.690
My dad passed away in
a motorcycle accident

00:06:00.323 --> 00:06:01.200
and he was drunk.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:03.000
He just always happened to be that guy

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:05.400
that would get away with whatever,

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:07.290
and just be fun and it's fine.

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:09.540
And it's like, it's fine
until it's not fine.

00:06:10.865 --> 00:06:15.865
- I have a text from my
brother who passed away.

00:06:15.969 --> 00:06:17.430
I've known him since I was like four.

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:19.020
We always called each other like,

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:23.973
that he's my brother,
but he's not biological.

00:06:24.946 --> 00:06:26.492
He went missing.

00:06:26.492 --> 00:06:29.904
His mom called me and said
that they couldn't find him,

00:06:29.904 --> 00:06:30.904
they didn't know where he was,

00:06:30.904 --> 00:06:31.737
he wasn't answering his phone.

00:06:31.737 --> 00:06:34.170
I had to drive around LA looking for him.

00:06:34.170 --> 00:06:35.880
I eventually found him in Santa Monica,

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:40.880
and then he was like
expressing that he, you know,

00:06:41.469 --> 00:06:43.768
he was thinking about committing suicide.

00:06:43.768 --> 00:06:46.910
So I took him home and
I was checking up on him

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:48.810
as much as I could,

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:52.140
and then the next day
he went missing again.

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:54.993
We found him, he had walked a little bit,

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:58.465
but he wasn't really
talking to me anymore.

00:06:58.465 --> 00:06:59.697
So I was like, okay, like,

00:06:59.697 --> 00:07:00.840
we need to take you to the hospital

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:02.040
and figure out what's going on.

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:04.530
I got a text from him
and he was just like,

00:07:04.530 --> 00:07:06.990
hey James, are you here?

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:10.140
I was just like, yeah, I'm
here, we're all here for you,

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:11.670
what's going on?

00:07:11.670 --> 00:07:16.670
20 minutes later, I got a
call from one of his friends

00:07:16.763 --> 00:07:21.090
saying that he jumped off the
building and he killed himself

00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:23.310
and his phone was on him,

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:27.453
and I never got a response
to the text I sent him.

00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:32.760
I don't know. Sometimes I
forget like that he is not here.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:35.100
Like, I'll have a dream
and then it'll feel real,

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:37.470
and then the next day
I'll like go to text him

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:39.320
and then I'll be like, wait, I can't.

00:07:41.001 --> 00:07:44.894
- So I met Vincent Nava
in my Freshman year.

00:07:44.894 --> 00:07:47.520
As a person, he was just so outgoing.

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:49.380
He never cool guy-ed anybody.

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:52.380
Like, he was the same person to everybody.

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:54.060
Favorite memory of him is probably

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:55.650
the last day I had with him,

00:07:55.650 --> 00:07:58.230
because I think I cherished it the most,

00:07:58.230 --> 00:08:00.030
'cause I didn't get to see him after that.

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:01.680
We went to my friend's house,

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:04.440
we were all getting
together, just friends.

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:07.170
There was actually a couple
pictures from the days before,

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:09.657
from another party,
and I sent them to him.

00:08:09.657 --> 00:08:11.820
And he was like, my family, I love you,

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:13.530
and I was like, I love you more.

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:14.730
He was like, where you at?

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:16.530
And I was like, (beep) my bad boo.

00:08:16.530 --> 00:08:19.560
I was like, literally with
my whole family came through,

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:20.550
I'm at my crib.

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:23.580
I'm gonna get ready right
now and head over, pull up.

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:25.740
And then he was like,
for sure on my way sexy.

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:27.840
And then I just gave him the heart eyes.

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:30.884
That was just like literally
the last day I gotta see him.

00:08:30.884 --> 00:08:33.780
And the next day he drove
to LA and then he swerved

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:36.450
and then he hit a back of a 18 wheeler

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:38.220
and he was in a coma for a couple days

00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:40.563
and he just never made it out.

00:08:42.432 --> 00:08:45.802
I just cherished those last
moments that I had with him,

00:08:45.802 --> 00:08:47.939
and I always have him on
my chain all the time,

00:08:47.939 --> 00:08:49.170
and I wear him every single day.

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:51.000
I don't ever take this off right here.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:53.815
- So I'm talking about my dad today.

00:08:53.815 --> 00:08:57.423
He passed away last year, last March.

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:00.210
He had terminal cancer.

00:09:00.210 --> 00:09:05.210
He and I were probably a lot
similar than I like to admit.

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:09.510
He was a professor, he taught art.

00:09:09.510 --> 00:09:13.740
But the last text exchange that we have,

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:18.090
I was on my way to go visit
one of my best friends.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:22.320
He texted me right before
I got on the plane.

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:24.900
Love you! Have a great trip.

00:09:24.900 --> 00:09:28.803
Learn from the world with
others dear to you, your pop.

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:31.980
And then I said landed!

00:09:31.980 --> 00:09:36.980
When he got sick, it
changed how he looked,

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:40.740
and so I don't really have
very many pictures of him

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:44.730
during that season, just
because he looked really sick.

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:49.230
And so I have some pictures
of us when I was little.

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:52.173
That's me when I was little,

00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:56.370
and that's my dad.

00:09:56.370 --> 00:10:01.233
I recorded his voice a lot,
so I have a lot of his voice.

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:03.113
- [Pop] Ellis, this is pop.

00:10:03.113 --> 00:10:05.330
I'm just calling to see
if you got there okay.

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:07.583
- That's it.

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:11.670
I think that's the thing I miss most

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:14.460
is having someone to come home to,

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:19.173
just a little voicemail to
check in and see how I'm doing.

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:21.848
- [Interviewer] Is there anything

00:10:21.848 --> 00:10:23.543
that you would want to say to her?

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:28.920
- I would just say that I
miss her. I miss you so much.

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:32.910
- One thing that comes to mind
is say, let's have a beer.

00:10:32.910 --> 00:10:34.260
I'd like to have, yeah,

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:36.260
I'd like to have one more beer with him.

00:10:37.890 --> 00:10:42.780
- I just miss you. And I
hope that you feel better.

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:46.650
I hope that you don't have that
stress of your body anymore.

00:10:46.650 --> 00:10:49.740
- I'm glad that I got to
show you that I loved you

00:10:49.740 --> 00:10:51.360
and that you knew that.

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:54.772
- I miss you and I love you very much,

00:10:54.772 --> 00:10:59.370
and I hope that you're
doing well wherever you are,

00:10:59.370 --> 00:11:02.553
and I hope you're happy.

00:11:03.450 --> 00:11:07.230
- Dealing with somebody that
passed away close to you

00:11:07.230 --> 00:11:09.240
is a rock of emotions,

00:11:09.240 --> 00:11:11.250
and it doesn't hit everybody the same.

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:13.710
And you know, sometimes
I'm just driving in my car

00:11:13.710 --> 00:11:14.940
and I'll be crying.

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:16.110
And like, it would just hit me

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:19.073
'cause I realize that I really can't see

00:11:19.073 --> 00:11:20.610
my best friend again.

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:22.380
There's no right or wrong way to do it,

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:25.617
just feel the emotions and go through it,

00:11:25.617 --> 00:11:28.770
and I would definitely
talk to people about it.

00:11:28.770 --> 00:11:31.860
- Focus on the community
you have around you,

00:11:31.860 --> 00:11:34.770
because so many people love you.

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:37.230
And I think it's just
about the little ways

00:11:37.230 --> 00:11:40.590
that you preserve them and
you keep them in your memory.

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:43.530
I think you just have to
continue to live for them

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:45.300
and there's gonna be really bad days,

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:47.040
and you're gonna miss them so much,

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:48.810
but then there's gonna
be really good days,

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:51.753
and you're just gonna know
that they're smiling at you.

